PRIVACY POLICY FOR HEXMERGE: REACH 2048!
Last Updated: March 27, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how Hexmerge: Reach 2048! ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and discloses information about you when you use our mobile application on iOS.

1. Information We Collect
To provide a smooth puzzle experience and track your progress, we collect limited data. We do not request access to your contacts, camera, or microphone.

a. Gameplay & High Scores: * Purpose: To save your current board state, high scores, and game progress so you can resume playing later.

Processing: This data is primarily stored locally on your device.

b. Usage Data & Diagnostics:

Purpose: To improve game stability and performance (e.g., ensuring the hexagonal grid renders correctly). We may collect anonymous crash reports.

Processing: This data is aggregated and not linked to your personal identity.

c. Device Settings:

Purpose: The App interacts with your device's haptic engine (vibrations) and audio settings for in-game sound effects.

2. Third-Party Advertising & Tracking
To keep Hexmerge: Reach 2048! free to play, we display advertisements provided by third-party networks, such as Google AdMob.

a. Identifiers (IDFA): With your permission, we may access your device’s Advertising Identifier (IDFA) to deliver ads that are more relevant to your interests.

b. App Tracking Transparency (ATT): In accordance with Apple's requirements, you will see a prompt asking for permission to track your activity across other apps.

Your Choice: You can tap "Ask App Not to Track" to decline.

Effect of Declining: You will still see ads, but they will not be tailored to your interests. The core game features will remain fully functional.

3. Data Sharing and Disclosure
We do not sell your personal data. We share anonymous, aggregated data with third-party service providers (like Google AdMob) solely for displaying ads and analyzing game performance.
For more details, please review the Google Privacy Policy.

4. Children’s Privacy
Hexmerge: Reach 2048! is a puzzle game intended for a general audience. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under the age of 13. If we learn that we have collected such data, we will delete it immediately.

5. Security
We take reasonable measures to protect your information. Since the game functions primarily offline, your puzzle moves and scores are not transmitted to our servers.

6. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by revising the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page.

